WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.160
So far, the Marvel Cinematic Universe has
been as unstoppable as a juggernaut.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.060
Of course, that has to be spelled with a lowercase
"j," because the X-Men villain Juggernaut

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.320
is one of many characters Marvel Studios doesn't
currently own the rights to.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.760
Losing Juggernaut isn't a big deal, but there
are some major superheroes Marvel Studios

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.310
desperately wishes they could include in their
films.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:25.800
Here's a look at some of the big name superheroes
Marvel Studios can't use.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.860
Professor X

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.330
Professor Charles Xavier is one of Marvel's
biggest characters, but thanks to the success

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.550
of 20th Century Fox's X-Men franchise, he's
off limits to Marvel Studios for the foreseeable

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.550
future.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.600
Which is too bad, because in the comics, he
plays a much larger role than simply mentoring

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.600
the X-Men.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.010
As a member of Marvel's Illuminati, he helps
shape events that affect the entire world,

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:50.080
and he's been known to help out the Avengers
from time to time as well.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.170
Not to mention all the times his goals come
into conflict with the plans of the other

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.760
superheroes, or when he straight up becomes
a villain.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.851
Alas, unless Hugh Jackman can jump back in
time and change some key contract deals, it

00:01:01.851 --> 00:01:06.400
looks like Xavier will never be able to play
in the MCU sandbox.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.400
Deadpool

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.190
Marvel has been in a weird position for years
now.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:14.520
Naturally, the company wants movies featuring
its characters to succeed and become popular.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.560
But in order to get the rights back, they
actually need those films to flop — which

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.090
would compel the rights-holders to sell those
characters back — without permanently damaging

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.090
the brand.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.860
That's how they eventually brought Punisher,
Ghost Rider, and Daredevil back into the Marvel

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.280
Studios fold.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.040
Oh, god.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:45.970
But any hopes of getting Deadpool back were
dashed in 2016 when Fox's cheeky R-rated superhero

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:49.420
comedy starring Ryan Reynolds became an international
blockbuster.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.470
Interestingly, one of the best aspects of
the movie was his hilarious interplay with

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.270
members of the X-Men.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:59.530
Imagine if he were in the MCU, and could riff
with Iron Man, Captain America, and the rest

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.970
of the Avengers, not to mention Spider-Man.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.579
You'll have to imagine it, though, because
Fox made so much money off Deadpool there's

00:02:05.579 --> 00:02:10.679
little chance you'll see him anywhere near
Marvel Studios for years to come.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:12.379
"Whoo!

00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:13.859
Superhero landing!"

00:02:13.859 --> 00:02:14.859
Wolverine

00:02:14.859 --> 00:02:19.260
The whole fate of both the Marvel Cinematic
Universe and Fox's X-Men franchise turned

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.050
on a whim of fate involving a very unlikely
figure: actor Dougray Scott.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:28.419
Most fans probably don't recall, but when
the first X-Men film was gearing up for filming

00:02:28.419 --> 00:02:33.159
in the late '90s, it was Scott who was actually
cast as Wolverine, not Hugh Jackman.

00:02:33.159 --> 00:02:37.560
Unfortunately for him, he had a schedule conflict
with Mission: Impossible 2 and had to drop

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.370
out of the film, leading Fox to instead offer
up the role to Hugh Jackman.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:45.299
We'll never know what might have happened
if Scott had played Wolverine, but we do know

00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:50.109
that the X-Men franchise has ridden the back
of Jackman's stardom for the past two decades.

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:55.579
Logan is Jackman's ninth film as Wolverine,
and if he is to believed, it will be his last.

00:02:55.579 --> 00:02:59.629
But even if he never suits up as Wolverine
again, his legacy is secure.

00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:03.519
And part of that legacy is the fact that his
massive popularity has ensured that pretty

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:08.120
much none of the characters in the X-Men universe
will be returning to Marvel Studios any time

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.120
soon.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.120
Mister Fantastic

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.650
Dr. Reed Richards is a man of science.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.799
So he doesn't believe in superstition, but
it certainly seems like some kind of curse

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:19.480
has fallen on the cinematic Fantastic Four.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:24.089
After two relatively lackluster films from
Fox, the team received a cinematic reboot

00:03:24.089 --> 00:03:27.900
in 2015 that was both a critical and commercial
bomb.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.200
That film's failure fueled rumors that Fox
and Marvel had secretly cut a deal to return

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.290
the Fantastic Four's film rights to Marvel
Studios.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:39.069
Both sides deny this happened, but you can't
blame fans for dreaming.

00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:43.730
After all, Mister Fantastic has played a key
role in almost every single major Marvel Comics

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:48.959
event ever, and is a natural counterpart to
MCU big brains Tony Stark and Bruce Banner.

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:52.719
And considering Fox clearly doesn't know how
to handle the character, getting him back

00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:55.269
where he belongs just makes sense.

00:03:55.269 --> 00:03:56.269
Silver Surfer

00:03:56.269 --> 00:04:01.319
As filmgoers saw in the Fantastic Four sequel,
the Silver Surfer is an alien who was empowered

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:05.329
by the world-eating Galactus, but rebelled
and chose to become a hero.

00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:09.419
He's a perfect fit for the MCU's cosmic side,
possibly fighting alongside the Guardians

00:04:09.419 --> 00:04:12.409
of the Galaxy against threats such as Thanos
or Ronan.

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:15.489
Or he would be, if Marvel Studios could use
him.

00:04:15.489 --> 00:04:19.370
But since they can't, there will simply be
a surfboard shaped hole in space where he

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:20.519
should be.

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:21.519
Bummer.

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:23.550
The rest of the X-Men and the FF

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:27.930
Wolverine, Professor X, and Mister Fantastic
might be the biggest characters Fox has the

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:31.400
rights to, but of course there are dozens
if not hundreds more.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:35.590
The rest of the X-Men and the Fantastic Four
would certainly fit in perfectly in the Marvel

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:40.030
Cinematic Universe alongside teams like The
Avengers, the Defenders, and The Guardians

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.270
of the Galaxy, and something like the Infinity
War event would be the perfect place to bring

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.430
everyone together.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.650
But as long as Fox is able to keep making
money with its X-Men films, though, it's unlikely

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:52.870
Marvel Studios will get the chance to play
with their own toys.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.980
And that means the biggest losers aren't the
folks at either Fox or Marvel, but the fans.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.400
"I'm pretty grossed out."

00:04:59.409 --> 00:05:00.409
Thanks for watching!

00:05:00.409 --> 00:05:03.380
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.899
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

